    <h2>What Is the Brownie Batter Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>The Brownie Batter Blizzard uses brownie batter pieces — similar to cookie dough pieces but with a darker, more intense chocolate flavor — blended with chocolate fudge sauce into DQ soft serve. The result is a double-chocolate Blizzard that sits between the lighter candy-bar flavors and the extremely rich <a href="/items/choco-brownie-blizzard">Choco Brownie Extreme Blizzard</a>.</p>
  <p>See all Blizzard options and 2026 prices on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a> or explore the <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard Treats category</a>.</p>

    <h2>Brownie Batter vs. Choco Brownie Extreme</h2>
  <p>These two are frequently confused. The key difference:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Brownie Batter Blizzard</strong> — Uses brownie batter-flavored pieces (unbaked texture) with fudge sauce. Sweeter, slightly chewy pieces.</li>
    <li><a href="/items/choco-brownie-blizzard"><strong>Choco Brownie Extreme Blizzard</strong></a> — Uses actual baked brownie pieces that are chewier and more chocolatey, combined with more fudge. Darker, more intense flavor profile overall.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you want a sweeter, dessert-adjacent chocolate Blizzard, choose Brownie Batter. If you want a darker, more intense chocolate experience, choose Choco Brownie Extreme.</p>
  <h2>Pair With</h2>
  <p>The Brownie Batter Blizzard pairs well with the <a href="/items/dq-cake-round-8inch">DQ Cake</a> as a shared dessert for two — order a Mini or Small while someone else has a cake slice. For a solo indulgence, it works great as a dessert following a <a href="/items/original-cheeseburger">cheeseburger</a> from the food menu.</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Brownie Batter Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>530</td><td>Medium chocolate intensity</td></tr><tr><td>Choco Brownie Extreme</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>510</td><td>Darker, more intense chocolate</td></tr><tr><td>Cookie Dough Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>590</td><td>Sweet baked-good, lighter chocolate</td></tr><tr><td>Oreo Cookie Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>420</td><td>Lightest of the chocolate options</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>First timer?</strong> Order a Mini (3.99) — it's 4–5 spoonfuls, perfect for a taste test before committing to a full cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Best size for one person:</strong> Small (4.79) at 530 calories hits the sweet spot of satisfaction without going overboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade option:</strong> Ask to blend in a hot fudge swirl for richer chocolate depth, or add extra mix-ins (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Check the flip:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down — if your crew doesn't flip it, it's free.</li>
    </ul>

